# ZyraVision Mobile — Testing

## Overview
Testing ensures reliability across the 5-layer architecture. Each layer has specific testing strategies and coverage requirements. Tests are described in Portuguese for consistency with user-facing context.

## Test Structure

```
test/
├── unit/
│   ├── domain/
│   │   ├── entities/              # Entity behavior tests
│   │   └── usecases/              # Use case logic tests
│   ├── data/
│   │   ├── repositories/          # Repository implementation tests
│   │   ├── datasources/           # Data source tests (mocked HTTP)
│   │   └── mappers/               # DTO <-> Entity mapper tests
│   ├── state/
│   │   └── notifiers/             # Notifier behavior tests
│   └── presentation/
│       └── viewmodels/            # ViewModel logic tests
│
├── widget/
│   ├── widgets/                   # Zy* design system widget tests
│   └── pages/                     # Page-level widget tests
│
├── integration/
│   ├── auth_flow_test.dart        # Login -> Dashboard flow
│   ├── camera_list_test.dart      # Camera listing and filtering
│   └── streaming_test.dart        # Stream start/stop flow
│
├── fixtures/                      # JSON fixtures for API responses
│   ├── cameras.json
│   ├── user.json
│   └── paginated_cameras.json
│
└── helpers/
    ├── test_helpers.dart          # Shared test utilities
    ├── mock_providers.dart        # Riverpod provider overrides
    └── fake_data.dart             # Factory methods for test entities
```

## Coverage Targets

| Layer | Target | Rationale |
|-------|--------|-----------|
| **Domain** (entities, use cases) | **90%** | Core business logic must be thoroughly tested |
| **Data** (repositories, mappers) | **80%** | Data integrity and mapping correctness |
| **State** (notifiers) | **80%** | State transitions and side effects |
| **Presentation** (viewmodels) | **70%** | Formatting and display logic |
| **UI** (widgets, pages) | **60%** | Key interactions and rendering |
| **Overall** | **70%** | Minimum acceptable coverage |

## Unit Tests

### Domain Layer

#### Entity Tests
```dart
// test/unit/domain/entities/camera_test.dart
import 'package:flutter_test/flutter_test.dart';
import 'package:zyravision_mobile/domain/entities/camera.dart';

void main() {
  group('Camera', () {
    test('deve criar uma camera com valores padrao', () {
      final camera = Camera(
        id: '123',
        name: 'Camera Entrada',
        status: CameraStatus.active,
      );

      expect(camera.id, '123');
      expect(camera.name, 'Camera Entrada');
      expect(camera.status, CameraStatus.active);
    });

    test('deve comparar igualdade por valor (freezed)', () {
      final camera1 = Camera(id: '1', name: 'Cam', status: CameraStatus.active);
      final camera2 = Camera(id: '1', name: 'Cam', status: CameraStatus.active);

      expect(camera1, equals(camera2));
    });

    test('deve criar copia com copyWith', () {
      final camera = Camera(id: '1', name: 'Cam', status: CameraStatus.active);
      final updated = camera.copyWith(status: CameraStatus.offline);

      expect(updated.status, CameraStatus.offline);
      expect(updated.name, 'Cam'); // unchanged
    });
  });
}
```

#### Use Case Tests
```dart
// test/unit/domain/usecases/get_active_cameras_test.dart
import 'package:flutter_test/flutter_test.dart';
import 'package:mocktail/mocktail.dart';

class MockCameraRepository extends Mock implements CameraRepository {}

void main() {
  late GetActiveCameras useCase;
  late MockCameraRepository mockRepository;

  setUp(() {
    mockRepository = MockCameraRepository();
    useCase = GetActiveCameras(mockRepository);
  });

  group('GetActiveCameras', () {
    test('deve retornar apenas cameras ativas', () async {
      when(() => mockRepository.getCameras()).thenAnswer((_) async => [
        Camera(id: '1', name: 'Cam1', status: CameraStatus.active),
        Camera(id: '2', name: 'Cam2', status: CameraStatus.offline),
        Camera(id: '3', name: 'Cam3', status: CameraStatus.active),
      ]);

      final result = await useCase();

      expect(result, hasLength(2));
      expect(result.every((c) => c.status == CameraStatus.active), isTrue);
    });

    test('deve retornar lista vazia quando nao ha cameras ativas', () async {
      when(() => mockRepository.getCameras()).thenAnswer((_) async => [
        Camera(id: '1', name: 'Cam1', status: CameraStatus.offline),
      ]);

      final result = await useCase();

      expect(result, isEmpty);
    });

    test('deve propagar excecao do repositorio', () async {
      when(() => mockRepository.getCameras()).thenThrow(
        const AppException.network('Sem conexao'),
      );

      expect(() => useCase(), throwsA(isA<AppException>()));
    });
  });
}
```

### Data Layer

#### Repository Tests
```dart
// test/unit/data/repositories/camera_repository_impl_test.dart
void main() {
  late CameraRepositoryImpl repository;
  late MockCameraRemoteDataSource mockRemote;
  late MockCameraLocalDataSource mockLocal;

  setUp(() {
    mockRemote = MockCameraRemoteDataSource();
    mockLocal = MockCameraLocalDataSource();
    repository = CameraRepositoryImpl(mockRemote, mockLocal);
  });

  group('CameraRepositoryImpl', () {
    test('deve buscar cameras da API e cachear localmente', () async {
      when(() => mockRemote.getCameras()).thenAnswer((_) async => [cameraDtoFixture]);
      when(() => mockLocal.cacheCameras(any())).thenAnswer((_) async {});

      final result = await repository.getCameras();

      expect(result, hasLength(1));
      verify(() => mockLocal.cacheCameras(any())).called(1);
    });

    test('deve retornar cache local quando API falha', () async {
      when(() => mockRemote.getCameras()).thenThrow(
        const AppException.network('Offline'),
      );
      when(() => mockLocal.getCachedCameras()).thenAnswer((_) async => [cameraFixture]);

      final result = await repository.getCameras();

      expect(result, hasLength(1));
    });
  });
}
```

#### Mapper Tests
```dart
// test/unit/data/mappers/camera_mapper_test.dart
void main() {
  group('CameraMapper', () {
    test('deve converter CameraDto para Camera corretamente', () {
      final dto = CameraDto(
        id: '123',
        name: 'Camera Entrada',
        status: 'active',
        createdAt: '2025-01-15T10:30:00Z',
      );

      final entity = CameraMapper.toEntity(dto);

      expect(entity.id, '123');
      expect(entity.name, 'Camera Entrada');
      expect(entity.status, CameraStatus.active);
      expect(entity.createdAt, isA<DateTime>());
    });

    test('deve mapear status desconhecido para unknown', () {
      final dto = CameraDto(id: '1', name: 'Cam', status: 'invalid_status');

      final entity = CameraMapper.toEntity(dto);

      expect(entity.status, CameraStatus.unknown);
    });
  });
}
```

### State Layer

#### Notifier Tests
```dart
// test/unit/state/notifiers/camera_list_notifier_test.dart
void main() {
  group('CameraListNotifier', () {
    late ProviderContainer container;
    late MockCameraRepository mockRepository;

    setUp(() {
      mockRepository = MockCameraRepository();
      container = ProviderContainer(overrides: [
        cameraRepositoryProvider.overrideWithValue(mockRepository),
      ]);
    });

    tearDown(() => container.dispose());

    test('deve carregar cameras no build', () async {
      when(() => mockRepository.getCameras()).thenAnswer(
        (_) async => [cameraFixture],
      );

      // Wait for the async build to complete
      await container.read(cameraListProvider.future);

      final state = container.read(cameraListProvider);
      expect(state.value, hasLength(1));
    });

    test('deve atualizar estado para loading durante refresh', () async {
      when(() => mockRepository.getCameras()).thenAnswer(
        (_) async => [],
      );

      final notifier = container.read(cameraListProvider.notifier);
      await notifier.refresh();

      expect(container.read(cameraListProvider).hasValue, isTrue);
    });
  });
}
```

## Widget Tests

### Design System Widgets
```dart
// test/widget/widgets/zy_button_test.dart
void main() {
  group('ZyButton', () {
    testWidgets('deve renderizar com texto correto', (tester) async {
      await tester.pumpWidget(
        MaterialApp(
          home: Scaffold(
            body: ZyButton(
              label: 'Salvar',
              onPressed: () {},
            ),
          ),
        ),
      );

      expect(find.text('Salvar'), findsOneWidget);
    });

    testWidgets('deve chamar onPressed ao clicar', (tester) async {
      var pressed = false;

      await tester.pumpWidget(
        MaterialApp(
          home: Scaffold(
            body: ZyButton(
              label: 'Salvar',
              onPressed: () => pressed = true,
            ),
          ),
        ),
      );

      await tester.tap(find.byType(ZyButton));
      expect(pressed, isTrue);
    });

    testWidgets('deve estar desabilitado quando onPressed e null', (tester) async {
      await tester.pumpWidget(
        const MaterialApp(
          home: Scaffold(
            body: ZyButton(
              label: 'Salvar',
              onPressed: null,
            ),
          ),
        ),
      );

      final button = tester.widget<ElevatedButton>(find.byType(ElevatedButton));
      expect(button.onPressed, isNull);
    });

    testWidgets('deve mostrar spinner quando isLoading e true', (tester) async {
      await tester.pumpWidget(
        MaterialApp(
          home: Scaffold(
            body: ZyButton(
              label: 'Salvar',
              onPressed: () {},
              isLoading: true,
            ),
          ),
        ),
      );

      expect(find.byType(CircularProgressIndicator), findsOneWidget);
      expect(find.text('Salvar'), findsNothing);
    });
  });
}
```

### Page Tests
```dart
// test/widget/pages/camera_list_page_test.dart
void main() {
  group('CameraListPage', () {
    testWidgets('deve mostrar lista de cameras', (tester) async {
      await tester.pumpWidget(
        ProviderScope(
          overrides: [
            cameraListProvider.overrideWith(() => FakeCameraListNotifier([
              Camera(id: '1', name: 'Camera Entrada', status: CameraStatus.active),
              Camera(id: '2', name: 'Camera Garagem', status: CameraStatus.offline),
            ])),
          ],
          child: const MaterialApp(home: CameraListPage()),
        ),
      );

      await tester.pumpAndSettle();

      expect(find.text('Camera Entrada'), findsOneWidget);
      expect(find.text('Camera Garagem'), findsOneWidget);
    });

    testWidgets('deve mostrar estado vazio quando nao ha cameras', (tester) async {
      await tester.pumpWidget(
        ProviderScope(
          overrides: [
            cameraListProvider.overrideWith(() => FakeCameraListNotifier([])),
          ],
          child: const MaterialApp(home: CameraListPage()),
        ),
      );

      await tester.pumpAndSettle();

      expect(find.byType(ZyEmptyState), findsOneWidget);
    });
  });
}
```

## Integration Tests

```dart
// test/integration/auth_flow_test.dart
void main() {
  group('Fluxo de Autenticacao', () {
    testWidgets('deve fazer login e navegar para o dashboard', (tester) async {
      // Setup mock API server or override providers
      await tester.pumpWidget(const ProviderScope(child: ZyraVisionApp()));

      // Find and fill login fields
      await tester.enterText(find.byKey(const Key('email_field')), 'user@test.com');
      await tester.enterText(find.byKey(const Key('password_field')), 'password123');
      await tester.tap(find.byKey(const Key('login_button')));

      await tester.pumpAndSettle();

      // Verify navigation to dashboard
      expect(find.byType(DashboardPage), findsOneWidget);
    });
  });
}
```

## Mocking Strategy

### Use mocktail (not mockito)
```dart
import 'package:mocktail/mocktail.dart';

// Mocks
class MockCameraRepository extends Mock implements CameraRepository {}
class MockDio extends Mock implements Dio {}
class MockSecureStorage extends Mock implements FlutterSecureStorage {}

// Fakes (for registerFallbackValue)
class FakeCamera extends Fake implements Camera {}
class FakeRequestOptions extends Fake implements RequestOptions {}
```

### JSON Fixtures
Store API response fixtures in `test/fixtures/` as JSON files:
```
test/fixtures/
├── cameras.json
├── camera_detail.json
├── user_profile.json
├── paginated_cameras.json
└── auth_token_response.json
```

Load in tests:
```dart
Future<Map<String, dynamic>> loadFixture(String name) async {
  final file = File('test/fixtures/$name');
  return jsonDecode(await file.readAsString()) as Map<String, dynamic>;
}
```

### Test Data Factories
```dart
// test/helpers/fake_data.dart
class FakeData {
  static Camera camera({
    String id = '1',
    String name = 'Camera Teste',
    CameraStatus status = CameraStatus.active,
  }) {
    return Camera(id: id, name: name, status: status);
  }

  static User user({
    String id = '1',
    String name = 'Usuario Teste',
    String email = 'teste@zyravision.com',
  }) {
    return User(id: id, name: name, email: email);
  }
}
```

## File Naming

| Type | Pattern | Example |
|------|---------|---------|
| Unit test | `{file}_test.dart` | `camera_repository_impl_test.dart` |
| Widget test | `{widget}_test.dart` | `zy_button_test.dart` |
| Integration test | `{flow}_test.dart` | `auth_flow_test.dart` |
| Fixture | `{entity}.json` | `cameras.json` |
| Helper | `{purpose}.dart` | `mock_providers.dart` |

## Running Tests

```bash
# All tests
flutter test

# With coverage
flutter test --coverage

# Specific file
flutter test test/unit/domain/usecases/get_active_cameras_test.dart

# Integration tests (on device/emulator)
flutter test integration_test/
```

## Rules

- NEVER skip tests for domain entities and use cases — they are the business core.
- NEVER use real API calls in unit or widget tests — always mock the data layer.
- NEVER leave test descriptions in English — use Portuguese for consistency.
- ALWAYS use `mocktail` for mocking (not `mockito`).
- ALWAYS create test data via factory methods in `test/helpers/fake_data.dart`.
- ALWAYS store JSON fixtures in `test/fixtures/` — never inline large JSON in tests.
- ALWAYS test both success and error paths in repository and notifier tests.
- ALWAYS test loading, data, and error states in widget tests for async data.
- ALWAYS override Riverpod providers in widget tests — never rely on real implementations.
- ALWAYS run `flutter test --coverage` before submitting a PR and verify targets are met.
